%% PARTIAL_SUCCESS Flow - Graceful Degradation in Fan-Out
%% Shows how partial failures propagate through the system
%% Example: Order Processing workflow — LineItem fan-out with dependent Payment
%% Updated: Feb 2026

sequenceDiagram
    participant LI1 as LineItem #1
    participant LI2 as LineItem #2
    participant LI3 as LineItem #3
    participant DLI as DiscoverLineItems
    participant VPay as ValidatePayment
    participant SPay as SubmitPayment

    Note over LI1,LI3: Fan-Out: 3 LineItems discovered

    rect rgb(200, 250, 200)
        Note over LI1: SUCCESS
        LI1->>DLI: ACK (externalId: ext-li-001)
    end

    rect rgb(250, 200, 200)
        Note over LI2: FAILED
        LI2--xDLI: Submit Error (validation failed)
    end

    rect rgb(200, 250, 200)
        Note over LI3: SUCCESS
        LI3->>DLI: ACK (externalId: ext-li-003)
    end

    Note over DLI: All children done (2 success, 1 failed)
    DLI->>DLI: Build FK Map:<br/>{li-001: ext-li-001, li-003: ext-li-003}
    DLI->>DLI: Set status: PARTIAL_SUCCESS

    Note over VPay: PARTIAL_SUCCESS satisfies dependency
    DLI->>VPay: Trigger with FK Map

    VPay->>VPay: Validate payment data
    VPay->>SPay: Submit payment (ACK required)

    rect rgb(200, 250, 200)
        Note over SPay: Payment submitted with available line items
        SPay->>SPay: ACK received
    end

    Note over LI1,SPay: Result: 2 of 3 LineItems processed<br/>Job Status: PARTIAL_SUCCESS

